  "question": {
    "text": "For the following reaction scheme, percentage yields are given along the arrow:\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/D-Tt5M3Htq0cQqaPF7hJCFlF29l-1T3jq1_FlYzGPkY.original.fullsize.png\">\r\n\r\n$\\mathbf{x} g$ and $\\mathbf{y} g$ are mass of $\\mathbf{R}$ and $\\mathbf{U}$, respectively.\r\n\r\n(Use: Molar mass (in $\\mathrm{g} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}$ ) of $\\mathrm{H}, \\mathrm{C}$ and $\\mathrm{O}$ as 1,12 and 16 , respectively)\r\n\r\nThe value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is ___.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1.62",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle mathsize=\"20px\"><msub><mi>Mg</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mover><mi>Mg</mi><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><sub><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></sub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><sub><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></sub><mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mrow><mi>Propyne</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mstyle></mrow></munder></mstyle></math><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/b25026a4-4733-473c-9ac7-d186e253f94b-image.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 147px;\" /></p><p>Now, one mole of propyne give, one mole of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>-butyne.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;moles of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>-butyne&nbsp;give one mole of hexamethyl benzene.</p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;of propyne give&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>54</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>-butyne&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mfenced></math> but given that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>75</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;yeild and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;to propyne.</p><p>The mass of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>-butyne formed&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.4</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>75</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.05</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>162</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>-butyne give&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>162</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;of hexamethyl benzene&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>yield</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>But given that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;yield, and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>05</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>-butyne</p><p>The mass of hexamethyl benzene formed&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.05</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>40</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.62</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
